      brandExamples: ["Yorvipath"],
      class: "Sustained-release PTH(1-34) prodrug parathyroid-hormone replacement",
      usedToTreat: "Chronic hypoparathyroidism in adults; it was not studied for acute postsurgical hypoparathyroidism and is initiated only after calcium is stabilized with calcium and active vitamin D.",
      description: "Palopegteriparatide is a once-daily subcutaneous prodrug that continuously releases bioactive PTH(1-34) for adult hypoparathyroidism. Unlike intermittent osteoporosis teriparatide pulses, its purpose is physiologic parathyroid-hormone replacement across the day, restoring renal calcium conservation, phosphate excretion and active-vitamin-D production while reducing reliance on high oral calcium and calcitriol.",
      mechanism: "PTH(1-34) is transiently linked to an inert PEG carrier by a cleavable TransCon linker. Physiologic conditions slowly release active PTH, which stimulates PTH1 receptors on renal tubular cells, osteoblast-lineage cells and other tissues. Signaling raises distal renal calcium reabsorption, lowers proximal phosphate reabsorption, stimulates renal 1-alpha-hydroxylase and allows regulated bone turnover, thereby increasing serum calcium and decreasing phosphate.",
