      nursingEssentials: ["Correct vitamin-D status and magnesium, stabilize albumin-corrected calcium at the label threshold, document calcium/calcitriol doses, renal function, stone history, skeletal radiation/malignancy risk and digoxin before initiation.", "Use one injection for the total daily dose, adjust gradually with frequent calcium checks, and give the written rescue plan for missed doses or interruption because abrupt PTH withdrawal can produce dangerous hypocalcemia."],
      keyLabs: ["Albumin-corrected or ionized calcium, phosphate, magnesium, 25-OH vitamin D, creatinine/eGFR, urine calcium, calcium-phosphate burden and digoxin concentration/ECG when applicable."],
