      class: "FGF23-neutralizing human IgG1 monoclonal antibody",
      usedToTreat: "X-linked hypophosphatemia in adults and children age 6 months and older, and FGF23-related tumor-induced osteomalacia in adults and children age 2 years and older when the causative tumor cannot be localized or curatively treated.",
      description: "Burosumab-twza is a subcutaneous monoclonal antibody that neutralizes excess fibroblast growth factor 23. In XLH and tumor-induced osteomalacia, too much FGF23 wastes phosphate through the kidney and suppresses calcitriol synthesis; blocking it restores tubular phosphate reabsorption and increases 1,25-dihydroxyvitamin D so rickets or osteomalacia can mineralize.",
