      boxedWarning: "High-yield warning context: current CRYSVITA labeling has no boxed warning. Concomitant oral phosphate or active vitamin-D analogs are contraindicated because severe hyperphosphatemia and nephrocalcinosis can result. Do not initiate when phosphate is already normal/high or in severe/end-stage renal disease. Monitor hyperphosphatemia, nephrocalcinosis, hypersensitivity, injection reactions and restless legs symptoms.",
      nursingEssentials: ["Stop oral phosphate and active vitamin D at least one week before initiation, verify fasting age-adjusted phosphate below normal, renal function, calcium, PTH and nephrocalcinosis status.", "Draw phosphate at the product-specific point in the dosing interval; titrating from a random post-dose value can overestimate baseline and cause unsafe dosing."],
