      description: "Navepegritide is a once-weekly prodrug that gradually releases active CNP(89-126) for children with achondroplasia. The released peptide activates NPR-B and counters excessive FGFR3-MAPK growth suppression at the growth plate. Its weekly interval distinguishes it from daily vosoritide, but it still requires open epiphyses and does not correct the causative FGFR3 variant.",
