      description: "Inclisiran is a long-acting double-stranded siRNA that reduces hepatic production of PCSK9 rather than binding circulating PCSK9 protein. A GalNAc ligand targets hepatocyte asialoglycoprotein receptors, allowing RNA-induced silencing complexes to cleave PCSK9 mRNA repeatedly and preserve LDL receptors for months.",
